From: Ming Qian <ming.qian@nxp.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Mar 2022 08:12:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec: export v4l2 buffer dma-buf

Export V4L2 buffers as DRM PRIME frames for sharing with other hardware.
Port of the upstream v2 submission to FFmpeg 8.1.2:
https://ffmpeg.org/pipermail/ffmpeg-devel/2022-March/294515.html

Keep the original format mappings, DRM contexts, get_format negotiation,
and software fallback. Local port adjustments:
- Rebase includes and buffer release onto 8.1.2's AVRefStruct lifetime.
- Finish descriptor/reference cleanup before requeue or reinit notification.
- Initialize export requests and all fd slots; export only decoder capture
  buffers with libdrm and a mapped format; close partial exports on fallback.
- Honor multiplanar data offsets and single-planar format fields; use
  allocated height for chroma offsets and hardware-frame dimensions.
- Check descriptor plane bounds and reference allocation failures.
- Set sw_pix_fmt, propagate rejected get_format negotiation, and advertise
  DRM PRIME hardware configuration only in libdrm builds.

Signed-off-by: Ming Qian <ming.qian@nxp.com>
---
